<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajit Singh of Ladwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajit Singh was the raja of Ladwa, one of the Cis-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> states under British protection after 1809. Despite this, he kept ties with the Sikh kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> and joined its side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> of 1845 to 1846. The British confiscated his state in 1846 and imprisoned him.</p></div>
